WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:05.240
Stranger Things fans suspected from the start
that El's number eleven tattoo meant she was

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.240
just one of several test subjects experimented
upon at Hawkins Lab.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.680
And Season 2 confirmed that with the appearance
of Kali, aka number Eight.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.860
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I want to delve deep into some hidden

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:22.610
clues you may have missed in Season 2 which
reveal secrets about more young people likely

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:27.830
abducted by Hawkins Lab for experimentation
and who may appear in Season 3 and beyond.

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:32.180
Obviously, I'll be discussing spoilers from
both seasons, so take care if you're not up-to-date.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:37.860
Kali and El's tattoos suggest there are at
least nine other test subjects in Project

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.149
MK Ultra.

00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:43.200
And given that the lost sisters, who spent
time together in the Lab's Rainbow Room, have

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.649
different powers to each other, with Kali
being able to cast illusions, we can assume

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:51.879
the other young people subjected to the Lab's
experiments may also have developed different

00:00:51.879 --> 00:00:53.250
abilities.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:57.520
Although Kali herself doesn't mention any
other Hawkins test subjects, Eleven learned

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:01.930
about her lost sister when she read her mother's
mind and investigated further with the files

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:03.540
her Aunt Becky gave her.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:08.159
And it's in those files that we get some glimpses
of news reports about abductions and missing

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:09.590
children and mothers.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:13.880
Kali's file was among those papers so it's
very likely that Eleven's mother thought those

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:17.810
reports were connected to Project MK Ultra
and the Hawkins Lab.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:22.950
The first file that Eleven flips past is a
news clipping about a Cleveland girl who's

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.700
gone missing in Indiana.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:30.079
The report states that a 16-year old junior-high-school
Honors student and girls-basketball team captain

00:01:30.079 --> 00:01:35.270
from Ohio went missing at some point after
leaving an Indiana junior-high gym to go back

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:37.039
to her bus that was returning home.

00:01:37.039 --> 00:01:40.939
There's no date on this clipping, but it's
eerie that this potentially has a connection

00:01:40.939 --> 00:01:45.290
to the ending of season 2 where we see the
Shadow Monster in the Upside Down looming

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.670
over the Hawkins Middle School gym.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:52.219
The news report also states that the girl's
father is a widower, so she has a missing

00:01:52.219 --> 00:01:57.159
mother, and her father describes her as a
genius and exceptionally strong for her age.

00:01:57.159 --> 00:02:02.009
This could mean her mother was experimented
on at Hawkins or elsewhere, and after leaving

00:02:02.009 --> 00:02:05.719
the MKUltra project, gave birth to a girl
with special gifts.

00:02:05.719 --> 00:02:08.929
The mother could have later died from the
effects of the experiments, but the Hawkins

00:02:08.929 --> 00:02:13.290
Lab learned about the gifted girl and abducted
her while she was visiting Indiana.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:17.160
There's also another intriguing possibility,
though, which is that the girl was actually

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:21.340
playing basketball at Hawkins Middle School
itself, where we know there's a portal that

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:25.540
both a Demogorgon and Eleven used to cross
between the Upside Down and the real world.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.930
Well, if this girl was gifted like Eleven,
she might have stumbled across the portal

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:35.310
and travelled to the Upside Down either willingly
or accidentally, where perhaps she got lost.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:39.629
Or maybe she even created that portal in Hawkins
Middle School in the first place?

00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:43.670
OK, so if that's not crazy enough yet, there's
more in the clipping.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:47.610
The news report continues, mentioning that
a girl matching the missing girl's general

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:51.129
description was later discovered wandering
around an Indiana suburb.

00:02:51.129 --> 00:02:53.380
There are various possibilities here.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:57.060
One is that this girl was abducted by the
Hawkins Lab but she escaped and they managed

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:01.200
to find her and take her back to the facility
before she got to safety.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.140
Another possibility is that the Hawkins Lab
guys arranged for a similar-looking girl to

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:08.830
be seen in the neighbourhood as a way of trying
to hide the fact that the real girl had gone

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:13.709
missing or they could simply have had Kali
use her powers to cast an illusion, making

00:03:13.709 --> 00:03:16.219
it look like the girl was still out there.

00:03:16.219 --> 00:03:20.319
Remember, they've done these kinds of things
before, for example, releasing a fake dead

00:03:20.319 --> 00:03:25.110
body for Will to cover up the fact that he'd
gone missing in the Upside Down.

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:29.090
Alternatively, another pretty far-fetched
possibility, which may have sped through your

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:33.709
mind if you're a fan of The Flash TV show,
is that the Upside Down is a replica of our

00:03:33.709 --> 00:03:36.569
world, just that's it's been corrupted by
the Shadow Monster.

00:03:36.569 --> 00:03:41.180
After all, we see the same buildings from
Hawkins in the Upside Down, so could there

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:45.480
have been doppelganger versions of people
somewhere in the alternate dimension, and

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:50.019
a doppelganger of the missing girl was sent
to our world from the Upside Down?

00:03:50.019 --> 00:03:52.800
OK, back to the other reports.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:57.170
Behind the Cleveland clipping is another one
that only has some very sparse details.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:02.319
The title appears to read "Another Girl Lost"
and you can see the words "go Police" mentioned

00:04:02.319 --> 00:04:06.659
in the tiny bit of the report which is showing,
perhaps suggesting that the Chicago police

00:04:06.659 --> 00:04:07.659
were mentioned.

00:04:07.659 --> 00:04:11.930
If that's the case, then it looks like a Chicago
girl has disappeared too.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:17.500
Another file which Eleven flicks past mentions
a baby boy abducted from a Memphis hospital.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:22.000
The circumstances reported around the abduction
are particularly suspect as the account states

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.930
that the boy went missing with a nurse who
turned up for work unexpectedly after being

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.380
off sick for a week.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:31.380
The article then states that the nurse was
discovered dead from a gunshot wound at her

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.300
house, but the boy was missing.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:37.990
It sounds like the nurse was probably used
by the Hawkins Lab or MK Ultra project to

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:41.650
abduct the boy and then she was killed to
avoid her squealing.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:45.960
The fact she was off sick and then suddenly
appeared at work may suggest she spent time,

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:51.090
either willingly or under coercion, at the
Hawkins Lab or another secret government facility.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:55.350
It seems like the MK Ultra project were looking
for the child's mother because she was probably

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:59.720
an ex-test subject and they needed the nurse
to find out when or where she was going to

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:00.790
give birth.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:04.440
The fact that the show's gone to the effort
of putting so much information and a photo

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:08.520
in this clipping makes me think this is another
gifted character which the showrunners could

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.880
be setting up to appear in a future season.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:16.099
There's also something intriguing in another
newspaper clipping just behind the baby boy

00:05:16.099 --> 00:05:17.099
article.

00:05:17.099 --> 00:05:20.460
If you look carefully, there's some text about
someone missing from San Diego.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:24.979
San Diego is, of course, in California, and
we know that two new main characters, Max

00:05:24.979 --> 00:05:29.490
and Billy, moved from California to Hawkins
in season 2, though we don't know where from

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.490
exactly.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:34.389
We do know that Billy has a lot of issues
though, some of which may be explained by

00:05:34.389 --> 00:05:38.880
his authoritarian, bullying father, but we
don't know anything about Billy's mother and

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.940
why his father is no longer with her.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:45.720
In some ways, Billy's introduction in season
2 was a bit sketchy and perplexing as he was

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:50.160
a real jerk pretty much the whole time, so
I do wonder whether the showrunners decided

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.810
to include him more for potential future storylines.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:56.759
And, in fact, the Duffer Brothers have said
that they wanted to have a 'human villain

00:05:56.759 --> 00:05:59.530
in the [show] that could disrupt the lives
of [their] characters.'

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:03.789
So, it's a long-shot, but I wonder if there's
any potential connection between Billy's mother

00:06:03.789 --> 00:06:08.490
and this possible missing child or person
in San Diego.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:12.009
There's also one more set of clippings which
are a bit more cryptic.

00:06:12.009 --> 00:06:15.300
One says a mother and daughter from Pawtucket
have gone missing.

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:19.039
There's also a picture of a young boy which
mentions a county hospital.

00:06:19.039 --> 00:06:23.379
And another article seems to talk about a
wave of disappearances of children and teens.

00:06:23.379 --> 00:06:27.440
At the bottom of the piece, there's mention
of the Gary Police Department and Gary is

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.849
a small city in Indiana, not far from Chicago.

00:06:29.849 --> 00:06:34.530
Now, I don't expect we'll see all of these
reported abductions or missing children in

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:35.530
future seasons.

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:39.830
Some of the children or adults may be dead,
long gone or not important for the overall

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:42.800
storyline the Duffer Brothers want to tell
in the show.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:46.760
Some may also just be random reports that
are unconnected to the Hawkins Lab.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:51.130
However, I do think that the missing baby
boy and the missing girls-basketball captain

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:55.750
are very specific and detailed reports that
I think we'll see feed into either season

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:57.729
3 or 4.

00:06:57.729 --> 00:07:01.430
By the way, if you cast your mind back to
Season 1, you'll remember that, when Hopper

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:05.900
was reading newspaper articles about Dr Brenner,
one of them mentioned six subjects coming

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:11.280
forward to give testimony about the Project
MK Ultra experiments, and alongside that there

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:15.190
was a picture of young women dressed in the
kind of hospital gown we see El wear when

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:16.960
she first escapes from the Lab.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:22.080
So, just as Terry Ives, who took part in the
MK Ultra Project, gave birth to a gifted daughter

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:26.069
in the form of Eleven, any of those women
in that photograph could also be the mothers

00:07:26.069 --> 00:07:30.000
of similarly gifted children who'll appear
in the show going forward.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.509
On top of that, given Kali's awesome power
to make people see whatever she wants them

00:07:35.509 --> 00:07:39.580
to, there's the possibility that Hopper's
flashbacks to his last days with his daughter

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:44.990
are merely memories of illusions the Hawkins
Lab made him see, and that really his daughter

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:49.199
Sara was also one of the children abducted
and experimented on.

00:07:49.199 --> 00:07:53.930
Something else I think is interesting is the
strong X-Men vibe to the show, which has been

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:56.830
clear since the very first episode.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:08:01.909
Eleven already has powers reminiscent of various
X-Men like Professor X, Magneto and Jean Grey

00:08:01.909 --> 00:08:06.979
and I wonder whether the Duffer Bros are considering
potentially teaming El up with multiple gifted

00:08:06.979 --> 00:08:10.350
individuals like Kali and others out there
who we've yet to meet.

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:15.140
I love how the seasons have developed so far,
but if the Shadow Monster is going to be an

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:20.440
ongoing big bad, at some point I imagine it
will take more than just what Eleven can currently

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:21.919
do to defeat it.

00:08:21.919 --> 00:08:26.020
It's possible that Eleven could continue to
power up, as she has done this season, but

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:31.060
it wouldn't surprise me if eventually the
monster's defeat ended up being a group effort.

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:36.080
So, what do you think about having more gifted
children or individuals showing up in future

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:37.760
seasons of Stranger Things?

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:42.070
And do you have any theories or predictions
on who they'll be and what powers they'll

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:43.070
have?

